:- module(constructor_function_ambiguity, [go/1]).
:- use_module(prelude).
:- chr_constraint go(any).

% 'atom' is a constructor here and a function in the prelude, which
% every module imports. The two are distinguishable — this module's is
% 'constructor_function_ambiguity:atom', the prelude's is
% 'prelude:atom' — so the declaration itself is fine and only a *bare*
% reference is ambiguous.
%
% The head below is such a bare reference: YCHR-20020. Arity does not
% save it (the constructor is 0-ary, the prelude function is 1-ary):
% constructors are name-only in the type system.
:- chr_type shape ---> atom ; compound.

go(atom) <=> true.
